+- `'json'`: Parse the value as JSON. A value that is not valid JSON stays a string:
+
+```js
+import queryString from 'query-string';
+
+queryString.parse('filter=%7B%22a%22%3A1%7D&bad=%7Bnope', {
+	types: {
+		filter: 'json',
+		bad: 'json',
+	},
+});
+//=> {bad: '{nope', filter: {a: 1}}
+```
+
+Note: With a `comma`, `separator`, or `bracket-separator` array format, the value is split before it is parsed, so use an encoded JSON value only with another format.
+
 Note: The `'boolean'` type also converts `'0'` and `'1'` to booleans, and treats valueless keys (e.g. `?flag`) as `true`.
 
